The window closed mid-PR on a change that touched no architecture at all: a
taint-analysis branch was in flight while two feature merges and three
tracker auto-syncs landed, and the doc hit 17 commits of distance. The gate
then failed a PR whose own diff was entirely unrelated to it.

Pre-flighting cannot prevent that. The check measures commit DISTANCE, so it
goes stale after your LAST commit rather than before your first (L35) -- the
failure lands on whoever happens to be holding an open PR when the counter
rolls over, which is a scheduling accident rather than a signal.

30 commits is roughly 6 days of headroom at dev's cadence, against ~3 before.

NOT FIXED HERE, and filed separately rather than widened into this change:
the counter is also advanced by commits that CANNOT invalidate the doc.
Tracker auto-sync commits touch only .agent/tracker*/.ops and never any
analyzed source, yet each one consumes window. Excluding them addresses the
cause; this addresses the symptom cheaply and buys room to do that properly.

No test or doc pinned the old value.

